.TH lst2asm 1 "2026 November 14" ""

.SH NAME
lst2asm \- Convert list file to assembly

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lst2asm
<input.lst> <output.asm>

.SH COPYRIGHT
CoreLAB is Copyright (C) 2026 by Pozsar Zsolt.

.SH DESCRIPTION
The lst2asm script converts a list file to an assembly file. It uses awk to
remove addresses and opcodes, and attempts to restore proper indentation. Note
that the indentation may not always be placed correctly, for example, if a label
is not followed by a colon (such as in the Intel 1973 syntax).
.PP
The script is useable on Unix-like operating systems.

.SH FILES
.TP
.B *.lst:
Input list file.
.TP
.B *.asm:
Output assembly file.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.
.TP
.B 1
Insufficient parameters.
.TP
.B 2
Missing dependency.

